<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Padishah Khatun</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1256">1256</a>–<a href="/years/1295">1295</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Padishah Khatun was a ruler of the Qutlugh-Khanid dynasty of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kerman">Kerman</a>, in south-eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iran">Iran</a>, and a daughter of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/qutlugh-terken-khatun">Qutlugh Terken Khatun</a>. She married the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ilkhan">Ilkhan</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abaqa-khan">Abaqa</a> and later <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gaykhatu">Gaykhatu</a>, and governed Kerman from 1292. After Gaykhatu's fall she was deposed and executed in 1295. She was also known as a poet.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/padishah-khatun.jpg" alt="Padishah Khatun" width="320" height="443" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Elmi Publishing Institute · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Padishah_Khatun_-_1956_drawing.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
